($t$Peltogyne floribunda$t$, $t$Peltogyne floribunda$t$, $t$Fabaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Fabaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 25 m. Commonly found in South America particularly in Brazil, Venezuela, Guyana, and Trinidad and Tobago, Purpleheart or Peltogyne floribunda is a semi deciduous tree that is a major source of purpleheart wood. The wood is extremely hard and heavy, strong, and highly durable. It is well known for its color, which is often purple. It is of high quality, thus highly valued and is relatively expensive. The wood yields an aromatic resin that has medicinal properties and used to produce a red dye for textile fabrics. Peltogyne floribunda has no known edible part but it has a wide range of other uses. Its bark is used for making canoes. It has an umbrella-shaped canopy and a straight, cylindrical, buttressed bole that can be up to 90cm in diameter and unbranched for up to 25m.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Purpleheart, pau-roxo, zapatero$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Fabaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": [], "resistenza_gelo": "bassa", "spaziatura_cm": null, "consociazio