($t$Phyllanthus emblica$t$, $t$Phyllanthus emblica$t$, $t$Phyllanthaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Phyllanthaceae. Portamento: Shrub. Altezza massima indicativa: 15 m. Emblic or Phyllanthus emblica is a slow-growing, deciduous tree popular for its edible fruit. It reaches a height of up to 18 m upon maturity and it has simple, light green, pinnate leaves. Its flowers are greenish yellow. Its bole is often twisted and about 35 cm in diameter. The fruits are usually made into desserts or jams. A plant with high tannin content, particularly its fruits, bark, and leaves, Emblic is a known traditional medicine for the treatment of a wide range of conditions like fever, constipation, cough, and asthma. Emblic is tolerant to drought and forest fire. Plants can be grown from seed, ring budding, or veneer grafting. Other common names include Indian Gooseberry, Amla, Aonla, Amloki, Nelli, Malacca tree and Dhatri.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Emblica, Indian Gooseberry$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Phyllanthaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": [], "resistenza_gelo": "bassa", "spaziatura_cm": null, "consocia